What each field means. Write them as short descriptive phrases, not sentences,
and keep each under 200 characters:

  audience  - who reads this, specifically. "second-year CS students who have
              not seen memory safety" is better than "students": the checkers
              compare the writing against this, so detail helps them.
  tone      - how it should sound. "informative, urgent", "warm and plain".
  detail    - how much: brief, moderate, or detailed.
  objective - what it should achieve. "drive awareness and patching".
  style     - constraints on the writing. "plain, no jargon", "technical".

Never invent a constraint the operator did not express. If they have not said,
infer it from the source and say that is what you have done.
